## Guidelines

1. **Be Specific**: Provide exact CSS selectors, not vague descriptions
2. **Prioritize**: Focus on selectors that yield the most business value
3. **Be Practical**: Recommend selectors that are stable and specific enough
4. **Consider Fallbacks**: Suggest alternative selectors if primary ones might fail
5. **Link Focus**: Pay special attention to navigation and link structures
6. **Business Context**: Prioritize elements containing company info, products, team, contact details

## Examples of Good Selectors

```css
/* Specific and stable */
header.site-header nav.primary-nav
footer#main-footer .footer-links
section#about .team-members
div[data-component="product-card"]
nav[role="navigation"]

/* Semantic and reliable */
main article.blog-post
section.services-list
aside.contact-info
.company-info .team-section
```

## Important Notes

- Return ONLY valid JSON, no additional text
- Be conservative with priority scores (reserve 9-10 for critical content)
- If you find JSON-LD or structured data, note it prominently
- Consider mobile vs desktop layout differences
- Note any anti-scraping measures you detect
